# Upper-limb vascular reasoning drafts

Ten original formative questions are bound to twenty complete right/left source
records in `content/upper-vascular-reasoning-pins.json`. They supplement, rather
than replace, the existing identification and teaching material. All remain
**draft revision 1**, requiring exact-revision radiologist review.

The questions distinguish named arterial transitions/branches, palmar-arch
contributions and superficial venous drainage. They use the existing geometry;
no vessel junction, lumen, patency, flow, variation, acquired-image visibility or
CT/MRI registration is established by a named surface mesh. The wording concerns
usual anatomy, not a diagnostic or procedural recommendation.

## Sources and commercial-use boundary

Factual references checked 24 October 2026:

- [UAMS: arteries of the upper limb](https://medicine.uams.edu/neuroscience/education/medical-school-courses/human-structure-module/anatomy-tables/artery-tables/arteries-of-the-upper-limb/): axillary, brachial and deep brachial questions.
- [TTUHSC El Paso: forearm and wrist](https://anatomy.ttuhscep.edu/musculoskeletal_system/forearm_tables.html): radial, ulnar, common interosseous and anterior interosseous questions.
- [UAMS: selected veins of the upper limb](https://medicine.uams.edu/neuroscience/education/medical-school-courses/human-structure-module/anatomy-tables/vein-tables/selected-veins-of-the-upper-limb/): axillary, cephalic and basilic questions.

The stems and explanations are newly written factual summaries. No table,
publisher question, figure, image, model, texture or font was copied from those
sites. Public availability of a reference is not a licence to redistribute its
assets. Existing model provenance, licence notices and release gates are
unchanged; this addition imports no new dependency or asset and incurs no fee.

## Scope and review

The source pin generator reproduces the entire displayed record, including its
official FMA/file identity, ordered memberships, bundle, source tree, geometry
bounds and source SHA-256. Runtime matching refuses a changed or additional
identity field; it does not match by name alone. Membership is not broadened to
make more questions available.

Answers and alternatives must be loaded, visible in the selected catalogue
scope and on the same side. The two axillary-vein targets have a thorax
membership but no authored alternative in that thorax-only scope, so the
question must remain unavailable there. Whole-body and the relevant upper-limb
regions can offer it. Absent, isolated or unloaded alternatives must not
be silently substituted from another region or side.

Review material includes the exact question, choices, explanation and sources.
Adding a question changes its teaching fingerprint; previous material cannot
be submitted as though it reviewed the new question. No existing clinical
approval is transferred, and no private review decision is written by this work.

Reviewer: check each usual-pattern statement, branch/drainage terminology,
laterality and source representation; confirm one defensible answer and suitable
alternatives in each available region. Correct variants and educational wording
before approval. Acquired CT/MRI/US relevance and patient-space synchronization
are separate review tasks, not implied by passing these quiz checks.

## Reproduction

From the prepared native candidate, run `npm run upper-vascular-reasoning:test`.
Its exact-parent comparison requires the sibling `PREPARED.json` and immutable
cf9b source checkout identified there. Preserve that historical role; do not
relabel another source as the old baseline. The check exercises unchanged prior
concepts/lessons, source mutation refusals, regional answer/skip/retry paths and
revision-bound Review refusal before storage. These focused checks do not
substitute for browser, accessibility, clinical or full-release acceptance.

The isolated draft is not installed or publicly deployed. The normal preview
must remain unchanged until the owner separately authorizes a cutover.
